{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4897328","formula":"C₂₁H₃₆O₅","hill":"C21H36O5","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":21.0,"H":36.0,"O":5.0},"names":{"en":"Betaenone b"},"descriptions":{"en":"Betaenone B, like other betaenones (A and C), is a secondary metabolite isolated from the fungus Pleospora betae, a plant pathogen. Its phytotoxic properties have been shown to cause sugar beet leaf spots, which is characterized by black, pycnidia containing, concentric circles eventually leading to necrosis of the leaf tissue. Of the seven phytotoxins isolated in fungal leaf spots from sugar beet (Beta vulgaris), betaenone B showed the least phytotoxicity showing only 8% inhibition of growth while betaenone A and C showed 73% and 89% growth inhibition, respectively."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":158750,"mass":368.5,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC[C@@H](C)[C@@H]1[C@]([C@H]2[C@@H](C[C@@](C[C@@H]2C(=O)[C@@]1(C)O)(C)O)C)(C)C(=O)CCO","inchikey":"PUZNAAVWFXQUDM-HBKHSIGZSA-N","iupac":"(2S,3R,4R,4aS,5R,7R,8aS)-3-[(2R)-butan-2-yl]-2,7-dihydroxy-4-(3-hydroxypropanoyl)-2,4,5,7-tetramethyl-3,4a,5,6,8,8a-hexahydronaphthalen-1-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"158750","atoms":62,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.384,"y":-2.957,"z":0.571,"el":"O"},{"x":-5.161,"y":-0.552,"z":-0.209,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.304,"y":-2.937,"z":0.905,"el":"O"},{"x":1.575,"y":2.626,"z":-0.724,"el":"O"},{"x":2.119,"y":3.728,"z":1.71,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.006,"y":0.347,"z":-0.428,"el":"C"},{"x":0.498,"y":0.497,"z":-0.869,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.453,"y":-1.113,"z":-0.685,"el":"C"},{"x":1.316,"y":-0.821,"z":-0.55,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.048,"y":1.348,"z":-0.992,"el":"C"},{"x":0.734,"y":-1.681,"z":0.605,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.97,"y":-1.32,"z":-0.737,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.775,"y":-0.31,"z":0.077,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.445,"y":1.132,"z":-0.348,"e